  "body": "Stacked on #4492 - do not merge before #4492.\n\n## What changed\n\nFollow-up of the pre-review of #4492. Four points of #4503.\n\n- `fold_chip` now paints the glyph alone when the state text does not fit. When not even the glyph fits and the state needs attention, it paints a warn bar at the chip's foot. Only a clean chip stays bare. A pane too short for the title still shows only the folded mark. The text stays in the tooltip.\n- The Browser chip counts the warnings of the cached toolpaths (\"4 warnings\"). It reads them as the tree row reads them. An operation with warnings is therefore not \"Up to date\" on the chip.\n- The decision file `docs/decisions/4483-pane-fold.md` says why a leaf with several tabs shows the state of its active tab only.\n- Tests for the blocked and the never-generated state on both chips.\n\nNo change to toolpaths, posts or the project file. No command, so no MCP tool.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft_ui_kit::fold::tests::a_short_pane_paints_the_glyph_alone_not_nothing` (full text, glyph only, warn bar, bare clean chip).\n- `camcraft_ui_kit::fold::tests::an_attention_chip_paints_a_state_below_its_title_at_every_height` (drives `fold_chip`, reads the painted shapes: a state text or the warn bar under the title) and `a_clean_chip_paints_no_warn_bar_and_no_warn_ink`\n- `egui_app::tests::pane_fold::a_never_generated_operation_shows_on_both_folded_chips`\n- `egui_app::tests::pane_fold::a_blocked_operation_shows_on_both_folded_chips`\n- `a_stale_operation_shows_on_the_folded_browser_chip` is changed: the seed has warnings, so the chip shows the exact count (a literal 89 pins the counter), not \"Up to date\". The blocked test now pins the exact text \"1 blocked · N warnings\", so the order is pinned.\n\n## Gate\n\nBase for the gate: `refs/remotes/qsmits/issue/4483-side-pane-fold` (head `1bca29cc9`), so that only the commits of this PR count.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base <that ref>` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui-kit -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: both green on head `137fbb13e` (review fix: warn bar, exact-text tests).\nThe `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes from 2032 to 2034. `camcraft-ui-kit` has one test more.\nNo snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nShort pane, Browser chip with one blocked operation. Before: the chip shows only the title. After: the chip shows the warning glyph.\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4507/before.png)\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4507/after.png)\n\nTall pane, blocked operation. Before: \"1 blocked\". After: \"1 blocked\" with the warnings count.\n\n![before blocked](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4507/before-blocked.png)\n![after blocked](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4507/after-blocked.png)\n\n## Known gap\n\nIn the light theme `warn_ink` is 1.92:1 on the chip ground (below 3:1). UI plan A (#4485) adds the `status_warn` token. The bar and glyph switch to it there. See the decision file.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full heavy lanes and the light lane (not needed at this stage; the PR is a draft).\n- A leaf with several tabs: this is a documented limit, not a change.\n\nChangelog: none (the chip belongs to #4492, which is not released)\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #4503\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
